
How to set up CGOS
------------------

The name CGOS refers to the "Computer Go Server", a specialized online
platform designed for computer programs to play Go against each other.
It was created by Don Dailey for the computer Go community to test,
develop, and rate Go-playing programs. CGOS manages game scheduling
automatically, allowing developers to connect their bots and have them
play a variety of opponents without human intervention. The server uses
the ELO rating system to evaluate the strength of bots. Programs connect
to the server using the Go Text Protocol (GTP). There are no provisions
for chatting with other users; CGOS is for computers only.

CGOS is a client-server-based system, so there is one server and possibly
many clients. If you are interested to set up a server, create a directory
on the machine the server should run on. I will refer to this directory
as <server-code>. Copy all files and subdirectories from the server-python
directory to <server-code>:
cp -rp server-python/* <server-code>
Then please follow the HOWTO in <server-code>.

If you are interested to let your bot play on the CGOS server, create
a directory on the machine your bot runs on (which may well be the
same machine the server runs on). I will refer to this directory as
<client-code>. Copy all files and subdirectories from the client-python
directory to <client-code>:
cp -rp client-python/* <client-code>
Then please follow the HOWTO in <client-code>.

